e\\\"` string with usage guidance; no equivalent in backlog_list response\\nsource: `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1686-1696`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 8**: `backlog_view` budget checked only when `section is None` at 1818-1829\\nverdic: VERIFIED\\nclaim: backlog_view budget guard applies only to full (section=None) requests\\nevidence: Read(server.py:1820-1831) \u2014 `if section is None: ... if _token_count(serialised) > _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET: return _build_over_budget_view(...)` \u2014 guard is inside `if section is None` block\\nsource: `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1820-1831`\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: _LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET global ceiling is not overridable by callers that need full data\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Add an opt-in `token_budget` parameter to `backlog_list` (and `backlog_view`) so callers can raise, lower, or disable the auto-pagination ceiling, and enrich over-budget responses with machine-readable withheld-count and budget-cause fields.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (expose budget as parameter; enrich over-budget messages; mirror to backlog_view) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description + accepted ACs confirmed against server.py source\\n2. Scope boundaries (server.py lines 60-66 constants, 1522-1535 halving loop, 1567 pagination dict, 1578 next_call, 1820-1831 view guard) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(server.py:55-68) \u2014 `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` at line 61; `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` at line 66; halving loop at 1531-1535; pagination dict at line 1567; next_call at line 1578; view guard at lines 1820-1831\\n3. External interfaces (FastMCP/Pydantic MCP tool surface; tiktoken cl100k_base; Annotated[int, Field(...)] parameter pattern) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(server.py:58-69) \u2014 tiktoken.get_encoding at line 68; Annotated[int, Field(...)] pattern used throughout existing parameters\\n4. Constraints (no cast()/object/Any; TypedDict or Pydantic required; no breaking change to callers omitting the new parameter) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: linting-exceptions.md \u2014 ANN401 must be fixed not suppressed; halving loop is hot path per item description\\n5. Existing system context (backlog_list and backlog_view source locations verified) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(server.py:1518-1582, 1680-1700, 1818-1836) \u2014 all structures confirmed at expected locations with minor line-number drift (+1 to +2) from subsequent edits\\n6. Verification expectations (fastmcp call commands constructable from CLAUDE.md testing patterns) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 \\\"Testing MCP Servers Against Fresh Source Code\\\" section with exact fastmcp call patterns\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- All conditions remain AVAILABLE \u2014 no refutations from fact-check\\n- Line numbers drifted by +1 to +2 from prior grooming (2026-04-13) but all code structures present and correct\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **_list_token_budget global ceiling is not overridable by callers that need full data** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Verified code audit 2026-04-12 \u2014 backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md (c11, c13)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-13)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Agents consuming `backlog_list` on large backlogs silently receive partial data when using `limit=0`. The only workaround requires knowing the total item count first (`count_only=True` then a second call with an explicit `limit`), which defeats the purpose of auto-pagination. The `backlog_view` budget shares the same root pattern and is a related P1 (#1664). Aligns directly with CLAUDE.md \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" rule: \\\"Never introduce hard-coded truncation or length limits on content that a consumer (human or agent) needs to read.\\\"\\n\\nEffort: Medium\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: migration tools, analytics exports, reconciliation scripts, any agent that needs the complete item list without a prior count query\\n- Bottleneck: `limit=0` callers against large backlogs silently see a partial world \u2014 no observable signal in the response distinguishes \\\"all items returned\\\" from \\\"budget-truncated partial set\\\" unless the caller explicitly compares `pagination.limit` to `pagination.total`\\n- Three pagination axes (`offset`/`limit`, `page`/`tokens_per_page`/`page_token_limit`, `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET`) make the contract opaque; a caller cannot determine from the signature which axis governs the response size for their call pattern\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Callers that need full data (migration, export, reconciliation) can pass `token_budget=0` to disable halving without needing a prior count query\\n- Over-budget messages become machine-readable: withheld count + pagination cursor are first-class fields, not inferrable only from `pagination.total - pagination.limit`\\n- `backlog_list` and `backlog_view` reach parity on over-budget signalling \u2014 `backlog_view` already emits `_over_budget`/`_usage`; `backlog_list` should too\\n- Pagination contract becomes self-describing: callers can inspect `budget_applied` to distinguish \\\"all returned\\\" from \\\"truncated by budget\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `limit=0` (auto-pagination mode), `backlog_list` should:\\n\\n1. Apply the token budget by default (`token_budget` defaults to `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400`).\\n2. When a caller passes `token_budget=0`, return all items without halving (no budget applied).\\n3. When a caller passes `token_budget=N` (positive integer), use N as the ceiling instead of the default.\\n4. When budget truncation occurs, the `pagination` dict includes `budget_applied: true`, `budget_ceiling: <N>`, and `withheld_count: <total - effective_limit>`.\\n5. The `next_call` hint, when present due to budget truncation, is annotated or accompanied by a `messages` entry that names the budget as the cause.\\n\\n`backlog_view` should gain an equivalent `token_budget` parameter that overrides `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` when provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `backlog_list` gains a `token_budget: int` parameter (`ge=0`, default `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET`; `0` means unlimited).\\n- The halving loop at `server.py:1530\u20131534` reads the resolved budget from the parameter rather than the module constant.\\n- The `pagination` response dict gains three optional fields: `budget_applied: bool`, `budget_ceiling: int | None`, `withheld_count: int | None` \u2014 present only when `limit=0` and budget logic ran.\\n- `backlog_view` gains the same `token_budget: int` parameter overriding `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`.\\n- All new structured response fields are declared as TypedDict or Pydantic model fields \u2014 no bare `dict`, `object`, or `Any`.\\n- No change to the behaviour of callers that pass `limit > 0` (budget is already bypassed for those calls today).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `backlog_list(limit=0)` with a large backlog returns `pagination.has_more=True` AND `pagination.budget_applied=True` AND `pagination.withheld_count > 0`.\\n\\n   Verify:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   FASTMCP_SHOW_SERVER_BANNER=false FASTMCP_LOG_ENABLED=false \\\\\\n   uv run fastmcp call \\\\\\n     --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" \\\\\\n     --target backlog_list \\\\\\n     --input-json '{\\\"limit\\\": 0}' | \\\\\\n   python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.loads(json.loads(sys.stdin.read())['content'][0]['text']); p=d['pagination']; assert p.get('budget_applied') and p.get('withheld_count',0)>0, p\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n2. `backlog_list(limit=0, token_budget=0)` returns ALL items (no halving) and `pagination.budget_applied=False`.\\n\\n   Verify:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   FASTMCP_SHOW_SERVER_BANNER=false FASTMCP_LOG_ENABLED=false \\\\\\n   uv run fastmcp call \\\\\\n     --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" \\\\\\n     --target backlog_list \\\\\\n     --input-json '{\\\"limit\\\": 0, \\\"token_budget\\\": 0}' | \\\\\\n   python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.loads(json.loads(sys.stdin.read())['content'][0]['text']); p=d['pagination']; assert not p.get('budget_applied') and not p.get('has_more'), p\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n3. `backlog_list(limit=0, token_budget=500)` returns a smaller slice than the default budget and `pagination.budget_ceiling=500`.\\n\\n   Verify by asserting `pagination.budget_ceiling == 500` in the response.\\n\\n4. `backlog_view` accepts a `token_budget` parameter and, when passed `0`, returns the full item without triggering the compact `_over_budget` fallback.\\n\\n   Verify against a large item (e.g., `selector=\\\"#1722\\\"`) by asserting `\\\"_over_budget\\\"` is absent from the response when `token_budget=0`.\\n\\n5. No new response field uses `Any`, `object`, or `cast()`. Verify with:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   uv run ruff check --select ANN401 plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py\\n   uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py\\n   ```\\n\\n   Both must exit 0.\\n\\n6. Existing callers passing `limit > 0` are unaffected: the `token_budget` parameter is ignored when `limit > 0` (budget was already bypassed in that path). Verify by asserting `pagination.budget_applied` is absent or `False` in a `limit=5` call.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Primary source | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` lines 59\u201365, 1522\u20131534, 1566\u20131581, 1680\u20131694, 1818\u20131829 |\\n| Related item | #1723 \u2014 `artifact_read` cannot stream large artifacts (same family: fixed-budget, no override) |\\n| Prior evidence | `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md` \u00a7c11, \u00a7c13 |\\n| Prior evidence | `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-ux-analysis-verified.md` \u00a7c1, \u00a7c2 |\\n| Type constraint rule | `.claude/rules/linting-exceptions.md` (ANN401 must be fixed, not suppressed) |\\n| MCP test pattern | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 \\\"Testing MCP Servers Against Fresh Source Code\\\" |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all required inputs are present\\n- Blocks: Any agent/tool that needs to call `backlog_list` with `token_budget=0` to enumerate all items for migration, export, or reconciliation. Also unblocks full parity with `backlog_view`'s over-budget signalling.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 two parameter additions (one to `backlog_list`, one to `backlog_view`), one halving loop change to read from the parameter, three new optional pagination fields, and typed model declarations for the new fields. No schema migration; no breaking change to existing callers.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 describes `backlog_list` `status` filter notes and body exclusion; does not describe token_budget but callers reading this file may need the new parameter documented\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` backlog operations section \u2014 describes `backlog_list` usage patterns; `token_budget=0` for full enumeration should be documented here once available\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING. All source locations verified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- Any caller using `backlog_list(limit=0)` against a large backlog receives new optional fields in `pagination` \u2014 callers that do not inspect these fields are unaffected (additive change)\\n- Any caller relying on `backlog_view` over-budget compact fallback \u2014 new `token_budget=0` path bypasses it; existing callers omitting the parameter retain current behavior\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:61` \u2014 `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` constant referenced in halving loop; after fix, parameter takes precedence when provided\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:66` \u2014 `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` constant; after fix, parameter takes precedence when provided\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1567` \u2014 `pagination` dict type \u2014 must accommodate 3 new optional fields\\n- Any TypedDict or Pydantic model defining the `pagination` response shape\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list` \u2014 adds `token_budget: int` parameter; halving loop reads from parameter instead of `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` constant; `pagination` dict gains `budget_applied`, `budget_ceiling`, `withheld_count` fields\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::backlog_view` \u2014 adds `token_budget: int` parameter overriding `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Design intent**: Expose the token budget ceiling as a caller-accessible parameter, add machine-readable budget-cause fields to the over-budget response, and align `backlog_list` with `backlog_view`'s existing `_over_budget`/`_usage` signalling.\\n\\n**Current implementation**: `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` (line 61) is a module-level constant with no parameter thread. The `pagination` dict (line 1567) contains only `offset`, `limit`, `total`, `has_more`. `next_call` (line 1578) contains no budget-cause annotation. `backlog_view` already has richer over-budget signalling (`_over_budget`, `_full_chars`, `_usage` at lines 1686-1696) \u2014 `backlog_list` has none.\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: DIVERGENT \u2014 `backlog_list` budget behavior diverges from the design intent in two ways: (1) the budget is not caller-accessible, and (2) the over-budget response lacks the signalling fields that `backlog_view` already provides. The CLAUDE.md \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" rule states callers must be able to control what they read, which the current `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` constant directly violates. The fix restores alignment by adding `token_budget` parameter and `budget_applied`/`budget_ceiling`/`withheld_count` pagination fields.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 \\\"Testing MCP Servers Against Fresh Source Code\\\" \u2014 fastmcp call examples may need updating to show `token_budget` parameter\\n- Any skill/agent documentation that describes `backlog_list` response shape or pagination contract\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The system allowed an information-hiding outcome (callers receiving partial data silently) that an expose-budget parameter would have prevented. The `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` constant exists and governs behavior but was never surfaced to callers. There is no mechanism that alerts a caller when their `limit=0` request was silently truncated \u2014 `has_more=True` is the only signal and it does not name the budget as the cause. A `token_budget` parameter with corresponding `budget_applied` / `withheld_count` fields in the response would have been the guardrail.\\n**Analysis Method**: Missing-guardrail classification \u2014 no 5-whys or 6-sigma required\\n**Scenario Target**: `backlog_list(limit=0)` callers against large backlogs \u2192 receive partial data with no budget-cause signal \u2192 add `token_budget` parameter + `budget_applied`/`withheld_count`/`budget_ceiling` response fields as the guardrail\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `server.py:60` \u2014 `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` \u2014 module-level constant, not present on the parameter surface of `backlog_list`\\n- `server.py:65` \u2014 `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` \u2014 same pattern for `backlog_view`\\n- `server.py:1522\u20131524` \u2014 `if limit > 0: effective_limit = limit` \u2014 explicit limit bypasses the budget entirely; caller must already know the item count to use this bypass\\n- `server.py:1530\u20131534` \u2014 binary-search halving loop uses `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` as hard ceiling; no parameter thread\\n- `server.py:1566` \u2014 `pagination` dict carries `offset`, `limit`, `total`, `has_more` \u2014 does NOT carry `budget_applied`, `withheld_count`, or `budget_ceiling`\\n- `server.py:1577` \u2014 `next_call` injected as a plain string when `has_more=True`; no annotation indicating the budget caused the truncation\\n- `server.py:1684\u20131694` \u2014 `backlog_view` already emits `_over_budget: True`, `_full_chars`, and `_usage` string when its budget fires \u2014 `backlog_list` has no equivalent\\n- `server.py:1818\u20131829` \u2014 `backlog_view` budget checked only when `section is None`; no override parameter\\n\\n---\\n\\n### RT-ICA (Planner)\\n\\nAPPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Add opt-in `token_budget` parameter to `backlog_list`; enrich over-budget messages with withheld count; apply same pattern to `backlog_view` |\\n| Scope boundaries | PRESENT | `server.py:59\u201365` (constants), `1522\u20131534` (halving loop), `1566\u20131577` (pagination dict + next_call), `1818\u20131829` (view guard) |\\n| External interfaces | PRESENT | FastMCP/Pydantic MCP tool surface; tiktoken cl100k_base; `Annotated[int, Field(...)]` parameter pattern already used throughout |\\n| Constraints | PRESENT | No `cast()`, `object`, or `Any`; new structured fields must use TypedDict or Pydantic models; halving loop is hot path \u2014 avoid O(N) allocations per iteration; no breaking change to callers that omit the new parameter |\\n| Existing system context | PRESENT | `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` at line 60 (module constant, not on parameter surface); `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` at line 65 (same pattern); halving loop at 1530\u20131534; `next_call` injected at 1577 with no withheld-count message; `backlog_view` already has `_over_budget` / `_usage` fields in its over-budget response (line 1684) \u2014 `backlog_list` does not |\\n| Verification expectations | PRESENT | `fastmcp call` commands constructable from CLAUDE.md testing patterns; pass/fail observable from `pagination` fields and `messages` list in response |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. From the project root, run:\\n\\n```text\\nFASTMCP_SHOW_SERVER_BANNER=false FASTMCP_LOG_ENABLED=false \\\\\\nuv run fastmcp call \\\\\\n  --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\" \\\\\\n  --target backlog_list \\\\\\n  --input-json '{\\\"limit\\\": 0}'\\n```\\n\\n2. Parse the outer JSON and inspect `pagination`: `total` will substantially exceed `limit` when the budget ceiling fires (budget fires when the full result set exceeds 4,400 cl100k_base tokens).\\n3. Confirm that the `messages` list contains no statement about how many items were withheld or that a budget ceiling was applied.\\n4. Confirm that `next_call` is present in the response (budget did fire) but contains no withheld-count annotation \u2014 it shows only `backlog_list(offset=N, limit=M)`.\\n5. Attempt to pass `token_budget=0` or `token_budget=99999` \u2014 FastMCP returns a validation error because the field does not exist on the tool's parameter surface.\\n\\nSee: `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1531-1535` (halving loop), line 1567 (pagination dict without budget fields), line 1578 (next_call without budget annotation).\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `server.py::backlog_list` \u2014 primary producer of the changed interface (P)\\n- `server.py::backlog_view` \u2014 secondary producer, parallel fix (P)\\n- `server.py::_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` / `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` \u2014 module constants, demoted from authoritative ceiling to default (C)\\n- `pagination` response dict \u2014 gains new optional fields (C)\\n- All `backlog_list` callers in agent/skill code \u2014 consumers, additive change only (C)\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u6\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md` \u00a7Q1, \u00a7Q3\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-ux-analysis-verified.md` \u00a7c1, \u00a7c2\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Agents consuming `backlog_list` against large backlogs silently receive partial data whenever the 10K-token MCP call ceiling is not already the tighter bound.\\n- `backlog_list` has three overlapping pagination axes (`offset/limit`, `page/tokens_per_page/page_token_limit`, `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET`) and a caller cannot tell from the signature which one wins.\\n- `backlog_view` has a separate `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` with the same opacity problem (verified at server.py:1827-1828).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:59` defines a module-level constant `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` that auto-paginates `backlog_list` by binary-search halving of the result set (lines 1520-1533). The budget fires **only when `limit=0`** \u2014 if the caller passes an explicit limit, the budget is bypassed.\\n\\nTwo related gaps:\\n\\n1. The 4,400-token ceiling is hard-coded and not reachable from the parameter surface. A caller that wants the complete result set (e.g., a migration tool, an analytics export, a one-off reconciliation) cannot disable the halving except by already knowing the exact `limit` to pass \u2014 which defeats the auto-pagination's purpose.\\n2. When the halving caps the result, the response does not clearly state \\\"you asked for more than budget; N items were dropped; here is how to get the rest\\\". The `has_more` flag signals that more exist, but the dropped count and the guidance to paginate are not first-class.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b1fb781f310eb58b5c2d5b27294684fdabbd58231a05a43bc69ed1888a39bab5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg4lJw\"}"}